f": "BomRef.7823518693677073.47528382073576847"}, {"ref": "BomRef.6180777004321268.6924503280461181"}, {"ref": "BomRef.2908678543650053.03558632212314916"}, {"ref": "BomRef.14627380497233677.9529634073441443"}, {"ref": "BomRef.7282958611926638.4861876485653843"}, {"ref": "BomRef.44332957994255506.8652121603337869"}, {"ref": "BomRef.7706478662308047.008024325131604781"}, {"ref": "BomRef.469175862225495.5353055201732844"}, {"ref": "BomRef.8491268226980472.9645550954654993"}, {"ref": "BomRef.925803416712316.7061512579376152"}, {"ref": "BomRef.5835566183632521.9968081117439596"}, {"ref": "BomRef.1336692734365197.4516235398320352"}, {"ref": "BomRef.6105266524950724.7062911864976887"}, {"ref": "BomRef.39249883271382313.8527172954782376"}, {"ref": "BomRef.9121603594006742.8593531453317547"}, {"ref": "BomRef.10211426110476973.702685402384399"}, {"ref": "BomRef.7450605164637838.40027554596383463"}, {"ref": "BomRef.7884200802139099.7032233645339973"}, {"ref": "BomRef.7717864709974754.551363868633802"}, {"ref": "BomRef.42245082556731905.4959095397322789"}, {"ref": "BomRef.5827631612725491.4518951777231447"}, {"ref": "BomRef.2594308431022193.14294200673267965"}, {"ref": "BomRef.20740415471552287.6898343479950665"}, {"ref": "BomRef.6372266373521456.9359443161324118"}, {"ref": "BomRef.9712121280284127.9762087139048282"}, {"ref": "BomRef.8373354399394846.6194302195198518"}, {"ref": "BomRef.21854179763235215.747478419424012"}, {"ref": "BomRef.5679202442563069.40841189730865746"}, {"ref": "BomRef.5263489788527447.3768982638518622"}, {"ref": "BomRef.91479380923601.5656143163390513"}], "metadata": {"timestamp": "2026-11-23T10:24:53.252335+00:00"}, "serialNumber": "urn:uuid:ea544bba-cc92-442a-ae95-e32b815dda69", "version": 1, "vulnerabilities": [{"affects": [{"ref": "BomRef.7717864709974754.551363868633802"}], "bom-ref": "BomRef.2830682363428745.3980196214900913", "description": "### Summary  On Windows, attacker-controlled content in a wheel's `.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt` can cause setuptools' legacy wheel installation path to create an `__init__.py` outside the requested `destination_eggdir`.  The attacker can influence the destination path, but not the contents of the created file.  ### Details  Tested setuptools commit:  `6ead555c5fb29bc57fe6105b1bffc163f56fd558`  Relevant source:  `setuptools/wheel.py`  SHA-256:  `359b7e0d5dd8c3135653abe08a8ed5dc0352eadfd7df22cb5e2b5303b7c3cafd`  The relevant call path is:  `Wheel(wheel_path).install_as_egg(destination)` \u2192 `_install_as_egg` \u2192 `_convert_metadata` \u2192 `_fix_namespace_packages`  A wheel can provide attacker-controlled content in:  `<distribution>.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`  The namespace value is eventually used approximately as:  ```python mod_dir = os.path.join(destination_eggdir, *mod.split('.')) mod_init = os.path.join(mod_dir, '__init__.py')  If mod is a Windows drive-qualified absolute path containing no dots, mod.split('.') preserves it as a single component. On Windows, os.path.join(destination_eggdir, absolute_component) discards the original base directory and resolves to the attacker-supplied absolute path. The existing wheel filename and ZIP traversal checks do not validate this metadata value before it is subsequently interpreted as a filesystem path.  ```markdown ### PoC  The reproduction was performed entirely inside a disposable temporary directory.  Layout:  ```text sandbox/     destination/     outside/     input/     canary.txt ```  A synthetic wheel was created containing:  `demo_pkg-1.0.dist-info/namespace_packages.txt`  whose content was the absolute path of:  `sandbox\\outside`  The real acquired setuptools implementation was then invoked:  ```python setuptools.wheel.Wheel(synthetic_wheel).install_as_egg(     sandbox_destination ) ```  The operation completed without exception.  Expected metadata was created under:  `sandbox\\destination\\EGG-INFO`  but setuptools also created:  `sandbox\\outside\\__init__.py`  The file did not exist before execution.  Its contents were:  ```python __import__('pkg_resources').declare_namespace(__name__) ```  The unrelated canary remained byte-identical.  The sandbox was deleted after recording the evidence. ```   ### Impact  A crafted wheel can cause setuptools to create a fixed-content `__init__.py` outside the intended installation directory at a filesystem path influenced by the wheel, with the permissions of the process performing the installation.  The demonstrated reproduction required the target parent directory to already exist.", "id": "GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w", "recommendation": "Upgrade"}], "$schema": "http://cyclonedx.org/schema/bom-1.4.schema.json", "bomFormat": "CycloneDX", "specVersion": "1.4"}
